  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.4.38 (forks 2.4.35) - FIX: Math/MathF.Log2, Cbrt, Asinh, Acosh, Atanh compile in kernels (musl libm ports; + IntrinsicMath.Log1P); FIX (WebGPU/WebGL): accurate f32 log/log2/log10; FIX (WebGPU): short-circuit branches meeting before the merge returned 0; PERF: ArgumentMapper no longer blows up browser AOT builds; FIX (WebGPU/WebGL): a call nothing implements fails to compile (was a silent 0). v5.4.37 (forks 2.4.34) - FIX (CUDA): AllocatePageLocked1D / CreatePageLockFromPinned bind the accelerator first (a page lock made off the accelerator's thread threw \"invalid device context\"); Wasm worker reuses kernel instances across dispatches. v5.4.36 (forks 2.4.33) - PERF (Wasm): a dispatch no longer copies every argument buffer into the linear memory and back out; buffers stay in place between dispatches and are written back only when something needs them (a 64-thread kernel over a 32 MB buffer: 12.5 -> 0.25 ms per launch). v5.4.35 (forks 2.4.33) - FIX (Wasm): disposing a buffer while work queued on it has not run yet no longer fails with RangeError: offset is out of bounds; the buffer is released after that work. v5.4.34 (forks 2.4.33) - FIX (WebGPU / WebGL): MathF.Sin / Cos / Tan accurate at any argument up to 102943 (were 2.7e-4 off at |x| = 2000; now within 1.2e-7 like CUDA / OpenCL / Wasm). PERF (CPU accelerator): a launch of a kernel with barriers or shared memory no longer wakes every runtime thread (about 15 ms per launch -> 1.7 ms for one group). FIX (all backends but Wasm; wrong rounding): a double converted to Half / bf16 / FP8 / FP4 rounds once, to the nearest value of the type, as System.Half does (was rounded to float first). FIX (WebGPU / WebGL Dekker and Ozaki doubles): a double outside the f32 range loaded with a wrong exponent (1e-300 as 1.6e-38); WebGPU doubles below 2^-79 lost their low 29 bits; (float)-0.0 was +0; a double at the f32 overflow edge became NaN; Ozaki (float)d tied the wrong way just past an f32 midpoint. PlaywrightMultiTest honors a test's declared timeout. v5.4.33 (forks 2.4.32) - FIX (CUDA, OpenCL, WebGPU, WebGL, Wasm; silent wrong results): a conversion into bf16, FP8 E4M3 / E5M2 or FP4 E2M1 rounds to the type (was the identity: (float)(BFloat16)x returned x). FIX (same backends; silent wrong results): Half / bf16 / FP8 / FP4 arithmetic results round to the type as the .NET operators do (were float-exact until a store; up to 4,085 of 4,096 Half products differed). FIX (WebGPU): emulated-f16 float -> Half rounds; native f16 division matches .NET. FIX (WebGL): FP8 / FP4 decoders keep -0. OpenCL: a kernel that fails to compile carries the build log in CLException. New tests on every backend: LowPrecisionRoundTrip_*, LowPrecisionArithmetic_*. See CHANGELOG.md.",
